---
import { Callout, CodeTabs, Icon, Link } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'

const settingsExamples = [
  { value: 'server', label: 'Language server', language: 'json', code: `{
  "lsp": {
    "dep-beacon": {
      "settings": {
        "checkVulnerabilities": true,
        "includePrerelease": false,
        "registryUrl": "https://registry.npmjs.org",
        "showUpdateDiagnostics": true
      }
    }
  }
}` },
  { value: 'inline', label: 'Inline hints', language: 'json', code: `{
  "inlay_hints": {
    "enabled": true,
    "show_other_hints": true
  }
}` }
]
---

<Docs title="Zed Extension" description="Zed features provided by Dep Beacon through the Language Server Protocol.">
  <header class="docs-page-header">
    <p class="docs-eyebrow"><span>03</span> / Editor guide</p>
    <h1>Your dependencies.<br />The Zed way.</h1>
    <p class="docs-intro">
      Native diagnostics, hovers, and code actions bring dependency intelligence into Zed. Open a manifest and
        start with the signals already in your editor.
    </p>
    <dl class="docs-facts">
      <div><dt>Integration</dt><dd>Language Server Protocol</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Setup</dt><dd>No settings required</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="install">
    <h2 id="install">Open a manifest and get started</h2>
    <ol class="docs-steps" role="list">
      <li><strong>Find Dep Beacon.</strong><p>Open the command palette, run <code>zed: extensions</code>, and
        search for <code>Dep Beacon</code>.</p></li>
      <li><strong>Install the extension.</strong><p>Use version <code>0.0.3</code> or newer for the diagnostics and
        bulk-update workflow in this guide.</p></li>
      <li><strong>Open your workspace.</strong><p>Start with <code>package.json</code>,
        <code>pnpm-workspace.yaml</code>, or <code>pnpm-workspace.yml</code>.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <Callout class="docs-note">
      <strong>Updating while a manifest is open?</strong>
      <p>Focus it and run <code>editor: restart language server</code> once. Closing and reopening the manifest
        also works.</p>
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="dashboard">
    <h2 id="dashboard">See what needs attention</h2>
    <p>
      Click Zed’s error and warning indicator, or run <code>diagnostics: deploy</code>, to see actionable dependencies
      from open manifests in one editable multi-buffer. Updates appear as warnings; security findings use warnings
      or errors according to severity.
    </p>
    <dl class="docs-reference">
      <div><dt>Dependency dashboard</dt><dd><kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>⇧</kbd> <kbd>M</kbd> on macOS; <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>
        <kbd>Shift</kbd> <kbd>M</kbd> on Linux and Windows.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Code actions</dt><dd><kbd>⌘</kbd> <kbd>.</kbd> on macOS; <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> <kbd>.</kbd> on Linux and
        Windows.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p>
      Hover a dependency for resolved ranges, npm tags, update targets, and vulnerability details. Dependency-name links
      open npm. Default and named pnpm catalogs resolve before analysis.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="updates">
    <h2 id="updates">Update one dependency, or the manifest</h2>
    <p>Place the cursor on an actionable dependency, then open code actions.</p>
    <dl class="docs-reference">
      <div><dt>Patch, minor, major, latest</dt><dd>Apply the selected target to one dependency.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Update all compatible dependencies</dt><dd>Apply available compatible targets without crossing a
        major version.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Update all dependencies to latest</dt><dd>Move to latest targets, which can include breaking
        major-version updates.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p>
      Bulk actions appear when the selected dependency has an applicable manifest edit. For a <code>catalog:</code>
      or <code>catalog:&lt;name&gt;</code> reference, the update edits its owning entry in
        <code>pnpm-workspace.yaml</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="npm-tags">
    <h2 id="npm-tags">Understand the tag as well as the range</h2>
    <p>
      npm can publish a version under a tag such as <code>next</code> while <code>latest</code> still points to an older
      version. If the existing range already accepts that newer version, Dep Beacon explains the difference without
      offering a no-op edit or downgrade.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="optional-settings">
    <h2 id="optional-settings">Keep the defaults, or tune the signals</h2>
    <p>
      Configure the language server under <code>lsp.dep-beacon.settings</code> in your Zed settings file.
      Enable inlay hints separately if you want compact version and risk labels beside each dependency.
    </p>
    <CodeTabs wrap={false} ariaLabel="Optional Zed settings" items={settingsExamples} />
    <dl class="docs-reference">
      <div><dt><code>checkVulnerabilities</code></dt><dd>Defaults to <code>true</code>. Adds OSV.dev vulnerability
        details to dependency analysis.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>includePrerelease</code></dt><dd>Defaults to <code>false</code>. Opt in to consider prerelease
        versions.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>registryUrl</code></dt><dd>Defaults to the public npm registry.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>showUpdateDiagnostics</code></dt><dd>Defaults to <code>true</code>. Set it to
        <code>false</code> to hide update warnings while keeping security findings and manifest errors
        visible.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p>Disabling update diagnostics keeps analysis, hovers, code actions, and individual or bulk upgrades available.</p>
    <Callout class="docs-note">
      <strong>Built around Zed’s native surfaces.</strong>
      <p>Dep Beacon uses the diagnostics multi-buffer, hover, and code-action menu. It does not add a custom panel
        or VS Code-style inline decorations.</p>
    </Callout>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="source">
    <h2 id="source">Follow the source</h2>
    <p>
      Explore the <Link href="https://github.com/santi020k/dep-beacon/tree/main/extensions/dep-beacon-lsp" newTab>Zed
        adapter</Link>
      and <Link href="https://github.com/santi020k/dep-beacon/tree/main/packages/dep-beacon-lsp" newTab>language
        server</Link>
      in the Dep Beacon repository.
    </p>
  </section>

  <nav class="docs-next" aria-label="Related guide">
    <Link href="/docs/pnpm-workspaces">Connect a pnpm workspace <Icon name="arrow-right" /></Link>
  </nav>
</Docs>
